  "question": {
    "text": "The Lassiagne's extract is boiled with dil <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> before testing for halogens because,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lduDZ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgCN</mi></math> is soluble in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4v7QQ",
      "text": "Silver halides are soluble in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uYsSx",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ag</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is soluble in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rlaVR",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi></math> are decomposed by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Lassaigne’s extract is first boiled with dil. HNO<sub>3</sub> to decompose cyanide or sulphide of sodium (NaCN or Na<sub>2</sub>S) formed during Lassaigne’s test. These ions would otherwise interfere with silver nitrate test for halogen.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>aq</mi><mo> </mo><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>aq</mi><mo> </mo><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>→</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>aq</mi><mo> </mo><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mi>HCN</mi><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo>↑</mo><mo>)</mo></math></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>aq</mi><mo> </mo><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>aq</mi><mo> </mo><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>→</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>aq</mi><mo> </mo><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mo>↑</mo><mo> </mo><mo>)</mo></math></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hence option D is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
